    {
      "id": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
      "type": "declaration",
      "label": "Primitive Port Layouts",
      "root": true,
      "position": {
        "x": -1400,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 260,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "surfaces",
          "key": "surfaces",
          "label": "surfaces",
          "direction": "output",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 165,
          "role": "surface",
          "allowedEdgeTypes": [
            "surface"
          ],
          "metadata": {
            "structural": true,
            "relationship": true,
            "role": "surface",
            "required": false,
            "repeatable": true,
            "behaviors": [
              {
                "trigger": "drag-create",
                "action": "create-node",
                "nodeType": "view",
                "targetPort": "root"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "data": {
        "intent": {
          "summary": "A working plan for how each primitive should place its inputs and outputs, and which handles chain to an obvious next node."
        },
        "declaration": {
          "defaultSurfaceId": "web",
          "surfaces": [],
          "interfaceContract": {
            "version": 1,
            "implicitRootPort": false,
            "excludedRelationships": [
              "glyph",
              "icon-view",
              "summary-view",
              "view-sequence",
              "port",
              "default-handle"
            ]
          }
        },
        "document": {
          "url": "github://mikemartinez1974/public/qa/primitive-port-layouts/root.node"
        },
        "glyph": {
          "kind": "icon",
          "name": "AccountTree"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
          "nodeId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "primitive-port-layouts-overview",
      "type": "view",
      "label": "Overview",
      "position": {
        "x": -820,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 440,
      "data": {
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail"
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "ownsContent": true
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Primitive Port Layouts\n\nA draft plan for setting up live primitives for first use: what ports each one should carry, where those ports should sit, and which handles are the \"obvious next step\" a person can drag to keep building.\n\n## The convention being proposed\n\n- **Inputs default to top or left.** Something flowing into a node reads top-down or left-to-right.\n- **Outputs default to bottom or right.** Something the node produces or hands off reads the same way.\n- **A \"next\" handle** -- the one a person is expected to drag repeatedly to build a sequence -- gets the most natural continuation side (usually bottom or right), so dragging it feels like moving forward, not backward.\n- **A terminal port** (nothing more to attach after it) doesn't need a next-affordance at all.\n- **Legacy or rarely-wired relationships** stay in the standard set rather than being deleted, but a graph can name specific ones it never wants offered via `interfaceContract.excludedRelationships` -- same mechanism node-template already uses.\n\n## Scope\n\nTen primitives actually render ports on canvas today: **Declaration, View, Content, Glyph, Port, Portal, Bridge, Membrane, Method, Event Handler.** The other six primitive docs (Field, Edge, Edge Class, Script, Specification, Surface) describe concepts rather than node types with their own port geometry, so they're left out of this pass -- say if that's wrong.\n\nEach of the ten gets its own node here: the port layout going in, and an open question where one exists. Nothing here is applied to the app yet -- this is the plan to react to."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
          "nodeId": "primitive-port-layouts-overview"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "primitive-port-layouts-glyph",
      "type": "glyph",
      "label": "Glyph",
      "position": {
        "x": -820,
        "y": 80
      },
      "width": 220,
      "height": 140,
      "data": {
        "glyph": {
          "kind": "icon",
          "name": "AccountTree"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
          "nodeId": "primitive-port-layouts-glyph"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "primitive-doc-declaration",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Declaration",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -80,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 820,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Declaration\n\n## Layout\nOne real relationship: `surfaces` -- output, repeatable. Every Surface (`web` today, a future `3d`, anything else) is a branch off this one port, each its own View -> View -> ... -> Glyph chain carrying its own `surfaceId`. Not a family of relationships, one relationship with many edges.\n\n`glyph` and `view-sequence` are dropped entirely -- not deprioritized, gone:\n- A Glyph is only ever reached by walking a Surface's chain to its end, so a direct Declaration -> Glyph shortcut is a second, competing path to the same thing. The Declaration keeps its own `data.glyph` as an inline fallback (data, not a port) for when there's no chain to derive one from.\n- `view-sequence` (\"first view\") is redundant now that Surfaces exist: a renderer only ever resolves one Surface, and falls back to `web` -- not to a separate \"first view\" relationship.\n\nThe rest of the structural set stays: `boundary-begin`/`boundary-end` keep their deliberate opposite-corner span (routing, not data flow). `landing-surface` and `port` are grouped as \"spawn a satellite node\" outputs. `default-handle` is low-traffic, delegation-only.\n\n## Language note\n`web` isn't just *a* surface, it's *the default* surface -- the one a renderer falls back to when nothing more specific is requested.\n\n## Open question\nDoes dropping `glyph`/`view-sequence` happen at the global `DECLARATION_RELATIONSHIPS` level (every Declaration stops offering them, the way `default-view`/`summary-view`/`icon-view` already did), or only as the recommended shape going forward? The earlier removal was global and caused zero breakage because every graph that used those ports had self-authored them -- worth checking whether that same safety net holds here."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
          "nodeId": "primitive-doc-declaration"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "primitive-doc-view",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "View",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 480,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 820,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# View\n\n## Layout\n- `root` -- top. Where the Declaration connects directly (first View in a chain), or where `sequence-in` receives from the previous View -- same side, same role.\n- `surface-delegate` -- left. A sideways branch out to Content, not a continuation of the chain.\n- `sequence-out` (\"next view\") -- right. The chain reads left to right, so continuing it goes right.\n\nNo port is needed for \"ends in a Glyph\": a Glyph is simply whatever `sequence-out` is dragged to on the last View in the chain. The chain-walk already enforces that a Glyph terminates it -- that's a chain-walk invariant, not a port."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
          "nodeId": "primitive-doc-view"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "primitive-doc-content",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Content",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1040,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 820,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Content\n\n## Layout\nOne port: `root` -- input, top. Terminal -- nothing drags out of it. Content is where a chain ends up, not where it continues from."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
          "nodeId": "primitive-doc-content"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "primitive-doc-glyph",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Glyph",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1600,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 820,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Glyph\n\n## Layout\nOne port: `root` -- input, top. Terminal by design -- the Glyph always ends a Surface chain."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
          "nodeId": "primitive-doc-glyph"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "primitive-doc-port",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Port",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 2160,
        "y": -400
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 820,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Port\n\n## Layout\n- `root` (interface socket) -- input, left.\n- `default-view` / `summary-view` / `icon-view` -- grouped bottom/right, as a group -- Port's own \"views.\"\n- `glyph` / `handle` -- top -- both low-traffic.\n- `landing-surface` -- right.\n\n## Open question\nPort still uses the old default-view/summary-view/icon-view trio directly instead of a single repeatable `surfaces`-style port. Declaration already made that jump. Should Port get the same treatment, or is its situation different enough to leave alone?"
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
          "nodeId": "primitive-doc-port"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "primitive-doc-portal",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Portal",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -80,
        "y": 500
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 820,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Portal\n\n## Layout\nOne port: `root` -- input, left. Portal doesn't birth any local nodes, so there's no output to place."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
          "nodeId": "primitive-doc-portal"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "primitive-doc-bridge",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Bridge",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 480,
        "y": 500
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 820,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Bridge\n\n## Layout\nOne real, directional port instead of today's fully generic five-handle fallback. A Bridge that imports receives from outside (input, left); a Bridge that exports hands something outward (output, right).\n\n## Open question\nShould the side be conditional on `data.bridge.role` (import vs. export flips which side it's on), or one fixed side regardless of role, the way every other primitive here does?"
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
          "nodeId": "primitive-doc-bridge"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "primitive-doc-membrane",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Membrane (Boundary)",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1040,
        "y": 500
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 820,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Membrane (Boundary)\n\n## Layout\n- `root` -- left (input).\n- `next` -- right (output). Continuing rightward reads as \"insert after,\" matching how a boundary sequence visually extends."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
          "nodeId": "primitive-doc-membrane"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "primitive-doc-method",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Method",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 1600,
        "y": 500
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 820,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Method\n\n## Layout\nOne real port: `invoke` -- input, left. Carries `dataType: 'method'`, only accepts `invokes`-typed edges. The generic five-handle fallback goes away entirely -- nothing else about Method is a connection point; its behavior lives in `data.source`.\n\n## Open question\nDoes Method ever need an output -- a return-value port, or a \"next method\" chain for composing behavior -- or is it correctly a dead end?"
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
          "nodeId": "primitive-doc-method"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "primitive-doc-event-handler",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Event Handler",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": 2160,
        "y": 500
      },
      "width": 500,
      "height": 820,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Event Handler\n\n## Layout\n- `action-method` -- output, right. Carries `dataType: 'method'`, only accepts `invokes`-typed edges, drags to a Method.\n- `trigger` -- proposed as a real input port (top or left) instead of staying data-only (`trigger.sourceNodeId`/`trigger.eventKey`) -- \"the Event that starts this.\"\n\nThe generic five-handle fallback goes away entirely.\n\n## Open question\nTurning `trigger` into a real port is a bigger structural change than anything else in this plan -- today it's just two data fields, not a connection. Worth doing for visual clarity, or does the data-only approach stay?"
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "primitive-port-layouts-declaration",
          "nodeId": "primitive-doc-event-handler"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
